ion": "The established branch framework maintained under a pollarding regime.", "topic": "Pruning & tree work"}, {"term": "Pollard shoot", "definition": "A shoot arising from a pollard head after repeated pruning.", "topic": "Pruning & tree work"}, {"term": "Pollarding", "definition": "A repeated pruning system in which branches are cut back to established pollard heads to produce a managed framework of shoots.", "topic": "Pruning & tree work"}, {"term": "Pollarding (P) (AS 4373)", "definition": "Crown-modification pruning system in which branches are repeatedly cut back to established pollard heads to produce a managed framework of shoots (AS 4373-2007).", "topic": "Pruning & tree work"}, {"term": "Porosity", "definition": "The proportion of soil volume occupied by pores.", "topic": "Roots, soil & below-ground environment"}, {"term": "Post-construction inspection", "definition": "Inspection undertaken after works to assess tree condition and confirm restoration or protection outcomes.", "topic": "Development, construction & tree protection"}, {"term": "Pre-construction inspection", "definition": "Inspection undertaken before works commence to document tree condition and site circumstances.", "topic": "Development, construction & tree protection"}, {"term": "Precision", "definition": "The degree of repeatability or consistency of a measurement.", "topic": "Measurement, inventory & field terminology"}, {"term": "Preliminary arboricultural report (PAR)", "definition": "Under AS 4970:2025, an early-stage report prepared during planning that identifies trees, records key attributes and provides preliminary advice to inform design and retention decisions.", "topic": "Development, construction & tree protection"}, {"term": "Preliminary cut", "definition": "An initial pruning cut used to remove branch weight before completing the final cut.", "topic": "Pruning & tree work"}, {"term": "Premature senescence", "definition": "Abnormally early ageing or death of leaves, shoots 