ition": "A tree established through natural regeneration following disturbance or land-use change.", "topic": "Urban forestry & tree management"}, {"term": "Remedial (restorative) pruning (H) (AS 4373)", "definition": "Crown-modification pruning intended to improve the structure and form of a previously damaged, declining or poorly pruned tree (AS 4373-2007).", "topic": "Pruning & tree work"}, {"term": "Remnant tree", "definition": "A tree retained from a previous vegetation community or land-use condition and surviving within a changed landscape.", "topic": "Urban forestry & tree management"}, {"term": "Removal cut", "definition": "A pruning cut that removes a branch at its point of attachment to the parent stem or branch.", "topic": "Pruning & tree work"}, {"term": "Replacement tree", "definition": "A tree planted to replace an existing tree that has been removed or cannot reasonably be retained.", "topic": "Development, construction & tree protection"}, {"term": "Residual risk", "definition": "Risk remaining after specified risk mitigation measures have been implemented.", "topic": "Tree risk & assessment"}, {"term": "Resilience", "definition": "The capacity of a tree to withstand disturbance and recover functional performance.", "topic": "Tree health, vitality & diagnosis"}, {"term": "Resin", "definition": "A sticky plant exudate produced by some species, often associated with defence or injury response.", "topic": "Defects, decay & disorders"}, {"term": "Resistance", "definition": "The capacity of a tree or tissue to resist penetration, infection, deformation or failure.", "topic": "Tree health, vitality & diagnosis"}, {"term": "Restoration pruning", "definition": "Pruning intended to recover an appropriate crown structure following damage, neglect or inappropriate pruning.", "topic": "Pruning & tree work"}, {"term": "Retrenchment pruning", "definition": "A staged reduction of crown dimensions intended to maintain a mature or declining tree while reducing lever