e, compaction, disease, poor aeration or other constraints.", "topic": "Tree health, vitality & diagnosis"}, {"term": "Root failure", "definition": "Failure involving structural roots or the root-soil system.", "topic": "Tree risk & assessment"}, {"term": "Root flare", "definition": "The visible enlargement at the base of a trunk where the stem transitions into major roots.", "topic": "Tree biology & anatomy"}, {"term": "Root hair", "definition": "A fine epidermal extension that increases the absorptive surface of young roots.", "topic": "Tree biology & anatomy"}, {"term": "Root investigation", "definition": "Investigation undertaken to determine root presence, size, depth, direction or condition.", "topic": "Development, construction & tree protection"}, {"term": "Root mapping", "definition": "The process of locating or estimating root position and distribution using excavation, detection or other techniques.", "topic": "Roots, soil & below-ground environment"}, {"term": "Root plate", "definition": "The structural root system and associated soil mass that contributes to tree stability.", "topic": "Roots / stability"}, {"term": "Root plate radius", "definition": "The approximate radial extent of the structural root-soil system considered in stability assessment.", "topic": "Roots, soil & below-ground environment"}, {"term": "Root plate tilt", "definition": "Movement or inclination of the root-soil plate associated with partial overturning or instability.", "topic": "Roots, soil & below-ground environment"}, {"term": "Root protection area", "definition": "A designated area intended to protect roots from disturbance or damage.", "topic": "Roots, soil & below-ground environment"}, {"term": "Root pruning", "definition": "The deliberate severance or removal of roots for a defined management purpose.", "topic": "Roots, soil & below-ground environment"}, {"term": "Root pruning cut", "definition": "A deliberate cut made to a root, usually for construction, infrastructure or